{% extends 'site/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Press kit · Retracoon{% endblock %}
{% block description %}Retracoon press kit: a turn-based 8-bit roguelike where your raccoon wears every item it finds. Fact sheet, screenshots, capsules, raccoon renders and clips.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="page"><div class="wrap">
<span class="kicker">Press kit</span>
<h1>Retracoon</h1>
<div class="prose">
<p class="quote">A turn-based 8-bit roguelike where your raccoon wears every item it finds.</p>
<p>Short version: <b>The raccoon roguelike where the loot is the look.</b></p>

<h2>About the game</h2>
<p><b>Retracoon</b> is a turn-based 8-bit roguelike for phones and PC. A raccoon walks an endless road through {{ counts.areas }} areas, fighting foes that show their next move and hunting for the boss that hides somewhere in each area. Every one of its {{ counts.items|number_format }} items is drawn on the raccoon, so by stage 30 it might wear a lid crown, laser eyes and a trash mech. Retreat in time and your raccoon keeps its level for the next run; push too far and you start over.</p>

<h2>Fact sheet</h2>
<table class="facts">
    <tr><th>Developer</th><td>Leroy, solo developer, the Netherlands</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Platforms</th><td>Android and iOS (free, one ad at launch, cosmetic skins). Steam for Windows, macOS, Linux and Steam Deck (paid, no ads)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Release</th><td>Phones 1 December 2026, Steam 15 March 2027 (planned)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Price</th><td>Free on phones, €4.99 on Steam (planned)</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Content</th><td>{{ counts.items|number_format }} items, {{ counts.sets }} sets, {{ counts.skills }} skills, {{ counts.areas }} areas, {{ counts.skins }} skins. Browse all of it in the <a href="{{ path('wiki') }}">wiki</a></td></tr>
    {% if support_email %}<tr><th>Contact</th><td><a href="mailto:{{ support_email }}">{{ support_email }}</a></td></tr>{% endif %}
</table>
</div>

<h2>Downloads</h2>
<p class="body">Free to use in coverage of the game. Clips are silent; screenshots are real gameplay with no added text.</p>
{% for g in groups %}
<h3>{{ g.label }}</h3>
<div class="downloads">
    {% for f in g.files %}
    <a href="{{ f.url }}" download>
        <span class="thumb">{% if f.image %}<img class="pix" src="{{ f.url }}" alt="" loading="lazy">{% else %}<span class="px" style="font-size:10px;color:var(--mist)">MP4 clip</span>{% endif %}</span>
        <span>{{ f.name }}<br><small>{{ f.size >= 1048576 ? (f.size / 1048576)|round(1) ~ ' MB' : (f.size / 1024)|round ~ ' KB' }}</small></span>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div></div>
{% endblock %}
